cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, or parts of its code, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NDM virsh KVM Backup Restore"
abstract: >-
  A single Bash script to back up a shut-off libvirt/KVM virtual machine (definition,
  local disks, UEFI NVRAM, emulated TPM state) without snapshots, prove the backup boots
  with a disposable test VM, restore it to its original paths or as a renamed copy, and
  manage the backups. Disks are compressed qcow2 images, compared with the original by
  qemu-img compare and recorded in SHA256SUMS; nothing existing is ever overwritten.
